nna it is targeting. Unlike physical attacks, jamming is completely reversible, once the jammer is disengaged, communications can be restored. Attribution of jamming can be tough because the source can be small and highly mobile, and users operating on the wrong frequency or pointed at the wrong satellite can jam friendly communications.* Similiar to intentional jamming, accidential jamming can cause temporary signal degradation. Accidental jamming refers to unintentional interference with communication signals, and it can potentially impact spacecraft in various ways, depending on the severity, frequency, and duration of the interference.\n\n*https://aerospace.csis.org/aerospace101/counterspace-weapons-101","rdfs:label":"Jamming - SPARTA","rdfs:seeAlso":{"@id":"https://sparta.aerospace.org/technique/EX-0016/"},"rdfs:subClassOf":{"@id":"d3f:SPARTAExecutionTechnique"},"skos:prefLabel":"Jamming"}]},"subtechniques":{"@context":{"rdfs":"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#","owl":"http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#","d3f":"http://d3fend.mitre.org/ontologies/d3fend.owl#","skos":"http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#"},"@graph":[{"@id":"d3f:EX-0016","d3f:attack-id":["EX-0016"],"d3f:top-level":["true"],"rdfs:hasSubClass":[{"@id":"d3f:EX-0016.01"},{"@id":"d3f:EX-0016.02"},{"@id":"d3f:EX-0016.03"}],"rdfs:label":["Jamming - SPARTA"],"skos:prefLabel":["Jamming"]},{"@id":"d3f:EX-0016.01","d3f:attack-id":["EX-0016.01"],"rdfs:label":["Uplink Jamming - SPARTA"],"rdfs:subClassOf":[{"@id":"d3f:EX-0016"}],"skos:prefLabel":["Uplink Jamming"]},{"@id":"d3f:EX-0016.02","d3f:attack-id":["EX-0016.02"],"rdfs:label":["Downlink Jamming - SPARTA"],"rdfs:subClassOf":[{"@id":"d3f:EX-0016"}],"skos:prefLabel":["Downlink Jamming"]},{"@id":"d3f:EX-0016.03","d3f:attack-id":["EX-0016.03"],"rdfs:label":["Position, Navigation, and Timing (PNT) Jamming - SPARTA"],"rdfs:subClassOf":[{"@id":"d3f:EX-0016"}],"skos:prefLabel":["Position, Navigation, and Timing (PNT) Jamming"]}]},"framework":{"framework_key":"spar